BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:3e6d1b4c696bde30b777@answerrank.local
DTSTAMP:20260919T051854Z
DTSTART:20260926T090000
DTEND:20260926T110000
SUMMARY:LAUNCH 1: Install and prove it works
CATEGORIES:AnswerRank Launch
DESCRIPTION:Nothing costs money today.\n\n1. git clone the repo onto your l
 aptop\n2. pip install -r requirements.txt\n3. python3 -m unittest discover
  -s tests     (expect 43 passing)\n4. python3 run.py tick --force         
       (watch the fleet run)\n5. python3 run.py budget-init                
 (then edit budget.yml with\n   YOUR real numbers - guesses give you a runw
 ay you cannot trust)\n\n6. Audit three businesses you personally know:\n  
  python3 run.py audit "<Name>" <City> --state <ST> --vertical hvac \\\n   
     --website <url> --report\n\nREAD THOSE REPORTS CRITICALLY. Would you p
 ay $997/mo for that?\nIf not\, that is today's real work - fix it before a
  stranger sees one.
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:LAUNCH 1: Install and prove it works
TRIGGER:-PT30M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:e1ef534046ced6dc0c97@answerrank.local
DTSTAMP:20260919T051854Z
DTSTART:20260926T130000
DTEND:20260926T143000
SUMMARY:LAUNCH 2: Pick your vertical and market
CATEGORIES:AnswerRank Launch
DESCRIPTION:Decide\, then commit. Specificity is what makes the email land.
 \n\nPick ONE vertical: hvac\, plumbing\, roofing\, dental\, or legal.\nPic
 k 2-3 metros. Mid-size beats huge - less competition\, same budgets.\n\nSu
 ggested: HVAC. Highest urgency\, highest ticket ($6-12k jobs)\,\nand the w
 orst AI visibility of any vertical tested.\n\nThen run 20 audits in it and
  look for the pattern:\nwhat do the VISIBLE businesses have that the invis
 ible ones don't?\n\nWrite that down. That is your expertise\, and it is wh
 at you say on calls.
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:LAUNCH 2: Pick your vertical and market
TRIGGER:-PT30M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:b7335169ae5fa3ca703c@answerrank.local
DTSTAMP:20260919T051854Z
DTSTART:20260928T180000
DTEND:20260928T184500
SUMMARY:LAUNCH 3: Buy the sending domain ($12)
CATEGORIES:AnswerRank Launch
DESCRIPTION:First money spent. Twelve dollars.\n\n1. Buy a SEPARATE sending
  domain - never your main one.\n   If it burns\, your real domain and clie
 nt email survive.\n   Pattern: <brand>-mail.com\, get<brand>.com\, <brand>
 hq.com\n\n2. Set up Google Workspace Business Starter ($7.20/mo\, 1 seat).
 \n   You need real authenticated sending\, not a free inbox.\n\nRunning to
 tal: $12 one-time\, $7.20/mo. That is the whole spend so far.
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:LAUNCH 3: Buy the sending domain ($12)
TRIGGER:-PT30M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:290ac7f8976849bf7010@answerrank.local
DTSTAMP:20260919T051854Z
DTSTART:20260929T180000
DTEND:20260929T190000
SUMMARY:LAUNCH 4: DNS - SPF\, DKIM\, DMARC
CATEGORIES:AnswerRank Launch
DESCRIPTION:The most important hour of the whole launch.\n\nIn your domain'
 s DNS:\n  SPF    TXT  @         v=spf1 include:_spf.google.com ~all\n  DKI
 M   TXT  (Google Admin generates this - enable it and paste)\n  DMARC  TXT
   _dmarc    v=DMARC1\; p=quarantine\; rua=mailto:you@domain\n\np=none is N
 OT enough in 2026. It must be quarantine or reject.\n\nVerify:\n  dig +sho
 rt TXT yourdomain.com\n  dig +short TXT _dmarc.yourdomain.com\n\nCompliant
  senders see ~89% inbox placement. Non-compliant see 22-34%\nfiltered or r
 ejected outright. This hour is the difference.\n\nWARMUP STARTS TOMORROW a
 nd runs two weeks. It gates everything else.
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:LAUNCH 4: DNS - SPF\, DKIM\, DMARC
TRIGGER:-PT30M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:6311c1202eff1c136dc6@answerrank.local
DTSTAMP:20260919T051854Z
DTSTART:20260930T180000
DTEND:20260930T184500
SUMMARY:LAUNCH 5: API keys + first real audits
CATEGORIES:AnswerRank Launch
DESCRIPTION:Put $15 of credit on the APIs. It goes further than you expect 
 -\na full 10-prompt\, 4-engine audit costs about $0.06.\n\n  export OPENAI
 _API_KEY=...\n  export ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=...\n  export SERPER_API_KEY=... 
        (free tier is plenty to start)\n\nThen re-run an audit and compare 
 it to the simulated one from day 1.\nThis is the first time you see REAL d
 ata about a real business.\n\nRunning total: $27 one-time\, $12.20/mo.
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:LAUNCH 5: API keys + first real audits
TRIGGER:-PT30M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:b92a976aaa3b23ff3eb3@answerrank.local
DTSTAMP:20260919T051854Z
DTSTART:20261003T090000
DTEND:20261003T110000
SUMMARY:LAUNCH 6: Build the prospect list
CATEGORIES:AnswerRank Launch
DESCRIPTION:Target 200-300 qualified prospects in your vertical and metros.
 \n\n  python3 run.py tick --force\n  python3 run.py prospects\n\nQualifica
 tion bar - all four must be true:\n  1. Visibility score under 55       (t
 here is a real problem)\n  2. A competitor is beating them    (there is a 
 real threat)\n  3. They have a website             (there is something to 
 fix)\n  4. They already spend on marketing (truck wraps\, ads\, real GBP)\
 n\nNumber 4 you check by hand. A business with no website and no marketing
 \nspend is not a cheap client - it is a client who never pays.\n\nLet the 
 auditor run overnight.
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:LAUNCH 6: Build the prospect list
TRIGGER:-PT30M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:90dc141ccc329411cda7@answerrank.local
DTSTAMP:20260919T051854Z
DTSTART:20261003T130000
DTEND:20261003T150000
SUMMARY:LAUNCH 7: One-page site + unsubscribe
CATEGORIES:AnswerRank Launch
DESCRIPTION:Keep it to one page. A logo is not what closes a $997 deal.\n\n
   - What it is\, who it is for\, the three tiers\, a booking link\n  - Pri
 vacy policy and terms (templates are fine)\n  - THE UNSUBSCRIBE ENDPOINT A
 T /unsubscribe\n\nThat last one is legally required and blocks sending unt
 il it works.\nWire it to the suppression list.\n\nFree hosting is fine: Gi
 tHub Pages\, Netlify\, Cloudflare Pages.
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:LAUNCH 7: One-page site + unsubscribe
TRIGGER:-PT30M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:4cd6eba6da33b1ff1733@answerrank.local
DTSTAMP:20260919T051854Z
DTSTART:20261005T180000
DTEND:20261005T184500
SUMMARY:LAUNCH 8: Stripe + booking link
CATEGORIES:AnswerRank Launch
DESCRIPTION:  - Stripe account\, verified\n  - Payment links for all four t
 iers: $297\, $499\, $997\, $1997\n  - A calendar booking link (Cal.com fre
 e tier works)\n\nPut the booking link in your email signature today.
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:LAUNCH 8: Stripe + booking link
TRIGGER:-PT30M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:742140a06a27659a7ac2@answerrank.local
DTSTAMP:20260919T051854Z
DTSTART:20261006T180000
DTEND:20261006T183000
SUMMARY:LAUNCH 9: Mid-warmup check
CATEGORIES:AnswerRank Launch
DESCRIPTION:Halfway through warmup.\n\n  python3 run.py send --dry-run\n\nC
 onfirm: DNS passes\, no preflight errors\, physical address set in\nanswer
 rank.yml. If anything is red\, fix it now - you send in four days.\n\nStil
 l warming. Do not start cold outreach yet.
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:LAUNCH 9: Mid-warmup check
TRIGGER:-PT30M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:b49a68b76143ff901ede@answerrank.local
DTSTAMP:20260919T051854Z
DTSTART:20261008T180000
DTEND:20261008T190000
SUMMARY:LAUNCH 10: FIRST SEND - 20 emails
CATEGORIES:AnswerRank Launch
DESCRIPTION:The business starts today.\n\n  python3 run.py send --dry-run  
    (confirm clean)\n  python3 run.py inbox --full       (READ ALL 20. Ever
 y word.)\n  python3 run.py approve\n  python3 run.py send --limit 20\n\nTw
 enty. Not two hundred.\n\nThe first 50 emails are a test\, not a campaign.
  If nobody replies\, the\nproblem is the subject line or the targeting - n
 ot the volume. Find that\nout for 50 emails\, not 500.
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:LAUNCH 10: FIRST SEND - 20 emails
TRIGGER:-PT30M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:a0d9dc0aa3c300ae14ef@answerrank.local
DTSTAMP:20260919T051854Z
DTSTART:20261009T180000
DTEND:20261009T183000
SUMMARY:LAUNCH 11: Ramp to 40/day
CATEGORIES:AnswerRank Launch
DESCRIPTION:  python3 run.py send --limit 40\n\nWatch two numbers daily fro
 m here:\n  bounces    must stay under 2%\n  complaints must stay under 0.1
 %\n\nEither one drifts up -> STOP SENDING. Verify the list. Re-warm.\nDeli
 verability is the one resource you cannot buy back.
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:LAUNCH 11: Ramp to 40/day
TRIGGER:-PT30M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:b8bc74193188a86ab850@answerrank.local
DTSTAMP:20260919T051854Z
DTSTART:20261012T180000
DTEND:20261012T183000
SUMMARY:LAUNCH 12: Ramp to 60-100/day
CATEGORIES:AnswerRank Launch
DESCRIPTION:  python3 run.py send --limit 60\n\nReplies should be appearing
  by now. Every reply gets an answer within\ntwo hours during the day.\n\nE
 xpected at this point: 1-3% reply rate. On 200 sent\, that is 2-6 replies.
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:LAUNCH 12: Ramp to 60-100/day
TRIGGER:-PT30M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:64e61bef1f414c8cc0e8@answerrank.local
DTSTAMP:20260919T051854Z
DTSTART:20261017T090000
DTEND:20261017T103000
SUMMARY:LAUNCH 13: Deliver to anyone who said yes
CATEGORIES:AnswerRank Launch
DESCRIPTION:Send the full report to everyone who asked\, and offer the 20-m
 inute call.\n\n  python3 run.py audit "<Business>" <City> --state <ST> \\\
 n      --vertical <v> --website <url> --report\n\nReview the report by han
 d before it goes. Every time\, for your first\nthree prospects. After that
 \, trust the fleet.
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:LAUNCH 13: Deliver to anyone who said yes
TRIGGER:-PT30M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:fc3b79bf9ecd9300da49@answerrank.local
DTSTAMP:20260919T051854Z
DTSTART:20261024T090000
DTEND:20261024T110000
SUMMARY:LAUNCH 14: Diagnose\, do not guess
CATEGORIES:AnswerRank Launch
DESCRIPTION:Thirty days. Be honest about the numbers.\n\n  python3 run.py d
 ashboard\n  python3 run.py budget\n\nTargets:   250 audited / 400 sent / 8
 -15 replies / 4-8 calls / 2-3 clients\nAcceptable: 150 audited / 250 sent 
 / 4 replies   / 2 calls   / 1 client\n\nONE client by day 30 puts you on t
 he pessimistic curve - which still\nclears $5k inside a year. That is a wi
 n\, not a disappointment.\n\nZERO clients is a signal\, not a failure. Dia
 gnose which step broke and\nfix ONLY the earliest broken one:\n\n  not del
 ivered -> DNS/reputation. Everything else is wasted until fixed.\n  no rep
 lies    -> subject line\, then targeting.\n  no calls      -> report not l
 anding. Lead with the competitor gap.\n  no closes     -> talk less. Show 
 the test log. Ask for the card.\n\nFixing the pitch while your email lands
  in spam wastes a month.
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:LAUNCH 14: Diagnose\, do not guess
TRIGGER:-PT30M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:065746fc7139fba7e526@answerrank.local
DTSTAMP:20260919T051854Z
DTSTART:20260930T193000
DTEND:20260930T194000
SUMMARY:AnswerRank: Email warmup (10 min)
CATEGORIES:AnswerRank Launch
DESCRIPTION:10 minutes. Keep the sending domain warming.\n\nSend 5-10 real\
 , personal emails from the sending address today - to\nyourself\, to frien
 ds\, to anyone who will reply. Replies are the signal\nthat builds reputat
 ion.\n\nDo NOT start cold outreach until day 18. Sending cold from a cold 
 domain\nburns it permanently\, and a burned domain is abandoned\, not repa
 ired.
RRULE:FREQ=DAILY;UNTIL=20261008T193000
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:AnswerRank: Email warmup (10 min)
TRIGGER:-PT5M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:38b39691abb345217ad5@answerrank.local
DTSTAMP:20260919T051854Z
DTSTART:20261012T063000
DTEND:20261012T065000
SUMMARY:AnswerRank: Morning ops
CATEGORIES:AnswerRank
DESCRIPTION:Your 20 minutes that keep the business moving.\n\n1. python3 ru
 n.py agents\n   -> any ERR twice in a row? investigate before anything els
 e.\n\n2. python3 run.py inbox --full\n   -> READ every draft. They go out 
 under your name.\n\n3. python3 run.py approve\n   python3 run.py send --li
 mit 40\n\n4. Check the reply inbox. Anything in there beats everything els
 e today.\n\nIf you only ever do this one block\, the business still runs.
RRULE:FREQ=WEEKLY;BYDAY=MO,TU,WE,TH,FR
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:AnswerRank: Morning ops
TRIGGER:-PT5M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:218ec477e7ccb62e0fac@answerrank.local
DTSTAMP:20260919T051854Z
DTSTART:20261012T121500
DTEND:20261012T122500
SUMMARY:AnswerRank: Reply check
CATEGORIES:AnswerRank
DESCRIPTION:10 minutes. Replies only.\n\nAnswer anyone who responded. Speed
  matters more than polish -\na reply inside an hour converts far better th
 an a perfect one tomorrow.\n\nIf they asked for the report:\n  python3 run
 .py audit "<Business>" <City> --state <ST> \\\n      --vertical <vertical>
  --website <url> --report\n\nSend it with one line: "Here it is - happy to
  walk you through it\,\n20 minutes this week?" 
RRULE:FREQ=WEEKLY;BYDAY=MO,TU,WE,TH,FR
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:AnswerRank: Reply check
TRIGGER:-PT5M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aaadb9325b4d6a669804@answerrank.local
DTSTAMP:20260919T051854Z
DTSTART:20261013T173000
DTEND:20261013T190000
SUMMARY:AnswerRank: Sales calls
CATEGORIES:AnswerRank
DESCRIPTION:Owners of home service businesses are reachable now -\noff the 
 tools\, not yet at dinner. This is the best calling window you have.\n\nPe
 r business/02_SALES_PLAYBOOK.md:\n  0-2 min   "How do people find you toda
 y when they don't know you?"\n  2-8 min   Share the report. Walk the test 
 log. Stop at the competitor row.\n            THEN SAY NOTHING. Let the si
 lence work.\n  8-12 min  The three causes: schema\, answer-shaped content\
 , GBP + citations.\n  12-15 min The offer. $997/mo. Ask for the card ON TH
 E CALL.\n\nDo not offer to "send a proposal". That is where these deals di
 e.\n\nClosed one?  python3 run.py win "<Business>" --plan growth
RRULE:FREQ=WEEKLY;BYDAY=TU,TH
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:AnswerRank: Sales calls
TRIGGER:-PT15M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:611016c5d252ea6e59ea@answerrank.local
DTSTAMP:20260919T051854Z
DTSTART:20261031T090000
DTEND:20261031T110000
SUMMARY:AnswerRank: Weekly deep work
CATEGORIES:AnswerRank
DESCRIPTION:Two hours. The only long block in your week - protect it.\n\n1.
  python3 run.py dashboard\n   Where are you against $5k? Which funnel step
  is weakest?\n\n2. python3 run.py prospects --stage audited --limit 30\n  
  Top up the list if it is thinning.\n\n3. Review any client report that we
 nt out. Would YOU pay $997 for it?\n\n4. Fix the weakest funnel number - a
 nd only that one:\n     not delivered  -> DNS/reputation. Stop sending. Fi
 x SPF/DKIM/DMARC.\n     no replies     -> subject line and targeting.\n   
   no calls       -> report is not landing. Lead with the competitor gap.\n
      no closes      -> talk less\, show the test log\, ask for the card.\n
 \n5. Ten minutes: write down what you learned about your vertical this wee
 k.\n   That accumulates into the expertise you sell.
RRULE:FREQ=WEEKLY;BYDAY=SA
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:AnswerRank: Weekly deep work
TRIGGER:-PT30M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:bc8c32173c73936b9da5@answerrank.local
DTSTAMP:20260919T051854Z
DTSTART:20260927T100000
DTEND:20260927T103000
SUMMARY:AnswerRank: Rest day - no business work
CATEGORIES:AnswerRank
DESCRIPTION:Deliberately empty.\n\nThe plan assumes you take this day off. 
 Six days a week is sustainable\nfor a year\; seven is sustainable for abou
 t a month\, and this business\nneeds the year.
RRULE:FREQ=WEEKLY;BYDAY=SU
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:b9928e723e44461c4eb1@answerrank.local
DTSTAMP:20260919T051854Z
DTSTART:20261107T111500
DTEND:20261107T120000
SUMMARY:AnswerRank: Monthly close + tax reserve
CATEGORIES:AnswerRank
DESCRIPTION:Monthly close - 45 minutes. Do not skip this one.\n\n1. python3
  run.py dashboard\n   python3 run.py budget\n\n2. Reconcile the ledger aga
 inst your bank and Stripe.\n\n3. MOVE 30% OF PROFIT TO THE TAX ACCOUNT. To
 day\, not later.\n   Money that sits in the main account gets spent.\n\n4.
  python3 run.py budget --profit <this month's profit>\n   Follow the split
  it gives you.\n\n5. Any client whose score is flat two months running: ca
 ll them.\n   They churn quietly\, and always before they complain.\n\n6. R
 e-read one report you sent as if you were the client.
RRULE:FREQ=MONTHLY;BYDAY=1SA
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:AnswerRank: Monthly close + tax reserve
TRIGGER:-PT60M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
